# Visualization Style

When the user asks for a visualization, mockup, wireframe, layout, screen preview, popup preview, or any "show me what it would look like" request, **default to ASCII wireframes (ASCII UI layout / ASCII diagram)**.

## Why

- Saves time and tokens compared to heavy canvas/fidelity mockups.
- Communicates layout intent clearly.
- Easy to edit, copy, paste, and diff.

## How to draw an ASCII wireframe

1. Use a fixed-width monospace block.
2. Draw the outer container first (e.g. browser frame, modal box, card).
3. Use ASCII box characters consistently:
   - `┌ ─ ┐` for top corners and top/bottom edges
   - `└ ─ ┘` for bottom corners
   - `│` for left/right edges
   - `├ ┤ ┬ ┴ ┼` for internal intersections when needed
   - `╔ ═ ╗` and `╚ ╝` for nested/highlighted boxes
4. Label each region explicitly (`[Header]`, `[Sidebar]`, `[CTA: Submit]`, etc.).
5. Show interactive states by switching only the relevant rows (e.g. button text, badge text).
6. Use arrows (`→`, `▼`, `↑`, `←`) to indicate flow, navigation, or state transitions.
7. Keep line length reasonable (≤ 100 chars) for readability.

## Standard ASCII frame templates

Browser frame:

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ● ● ●   arsplatform.com/auth/google/callback                      │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                   │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Modal / popup:

```text
╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ Choose your requested role                                    [X] ║
╠═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║ ( ) Researcher     Submit manuscripts and manage research work.   ║
║ ( ) Reviewer       Evaluate papers and manage assigned reviews.   ║
║ ( ) Lecturer       Manage seminars and student guidance.          ║
╠═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║                            [ Cancel ]  [ Continue ]               ║
╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

Card / form section:

```text
┌─ Upload verification PDF ─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                   │
│      ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐          │
│      │   Drop PDF here or choose a file                │          │
│      │   PDF only · 1 file · max 10MB                  │          │
│      └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘          │
│                                                                   │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Multi-state mockups

For a flow with multiple states, present them as **stacked labeled blocks**:

```text
[State 1: New user lands on role picker]
┌─ Choose your requested role ──────────────────────────────────────┐
...
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
[State 2: PDF uploaded, submit enabled]
┌─ Upload verification PDF ─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   ✓ verification-profile.pdf · 1.8MB                              │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
[State 3: Pending admin review]
┌─ Request submitted ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   [Pending review]   Continue to Forum →                          │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## When NOT to use ASCII

Use a richer canvas only when the user explicitly asks for:
- "high-fidelity mockup", "pixel-perfect", "interactive prototype", "build it", or
- provides screenshots/design specs to match.

In those cases, still consider an ASCII pass first to confirm layout before spending tokens on a canvas.

## Out of scope

- Do not paste code frameworks instead of a wireframe unless asked.
- Do not use emojis as UI controls in the wireframe.
- Do not include placeholder lorem text — short descriptive labels are enough.
